== Rule changes and innovations ==

The 2025–26 season features several notable updates and innovations:
* Adidas became the new official match ball supplier for the Süper Lig, succeeding Puma after a 3-year partnership.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|last1=Rest |first1=Jonathan |title=Adidas adds Turkish FA to incoming DFL ball deal |url=https://www.sportbusiness.com/news/adidas-adds-tff-to-incoming-dfl-ball-deal/ |website=SportBusiness |access-date=10 September 2025 |date=22 July 2025}}</ref><ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=Türkiye Profesyonel Ligleri Resmi Top Sponsoru adidas Oldu – TFF Haberleri TFF |url=https://www.tff.org/default.aspx?pageID=285&ftxtID=48014 |website=www.tff.org |publisher=Turkish Football Federation |access-date=10 September 2025 |language=tr |date=21 July 2025}}</ref>
* Clubs will be allowed to have a maximum of 14 foreign players on their rosters.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=TFF announces 14 foreign player limit for 2025–2026 Super Lig season |url=https://www.turkiyetoday.com/sports/tff-announces-14-foreign-player-limit-for-2025-2026-super-lig-season-147007 |website=Türkiye Today |publisher=Türkiye Today |access-date=10 September 2025 |language=en |date=19 April 2025}}</ref> Unlike previous seasons, the TFF has now introduced an age limit. Looking ahead to the 2026–27 season, at least 4 of the 14 foreign players must be born on or after 1 January 2004.
* On 13 August 2025, the TFF has officially launched the use of body cameras by the referee and fourth officials in the Süper Lig and [[TFF 1. Lig|TFF First League]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=Trendyol Süper Lig ve 1. Lig'de Aselsan Odakan Yaka Kamerası Dönemi Başladı – TFF Haberleri TFF |url=https://www.tff.org/default.aspx?pageID=285&ftxtID=48133 |website=www.tff.org |access-date=10 October 2025 |language=tr |date=13 August 2025}}</ref>

